	(footprint "W0525AB001D_Lands"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "99f409ce-885c-4534-b7d5-3eb5141bb8d0")
		(at 57.650783 79.93)
		(descr "Lands for the two lead wires of the Jinlong W0525AB001D coin vibration motor (5.0 dia x 2.5, BLDC, 3.0 V). Source: design/datasheets/slim2_jinlong-w0525ab001d.pdf page 9 (drawing): 'Lead Wire (AWG32) Red(+)' and 'Black(or Blue)(-)', lead length 30 +-1.5, stripped end 1.5 +-0.5; page 14 item 9-2 (red to +, blue or black to -). Pad 1 = red lead (+, net VMOT, ring netlist M1 pin 1) at the foot side, pad 2 = blue lead (-, net GND, M1 pin 2) 1.0 mm nearer the head. Each land is 0.30 along the tail x 0.80 across (long side toward the motor, which stands on the +X side of the tail). One AWG32 lead (bare diameter 0.20 mm) arrives across the tail from the motor, is stripped 0.6 mm and laid along the 0.80 side, then soldered by hand; pad centre is 0.13 mm toward -y of the footprint origin (FLEX1 frame, y = -v).")
